{"abstract":[{"text":"This parameter defines the range for the fade-out effect before an automatic content cutoff on pitched map views. Fade out is implemented by scaling down and removing buildings in the fade range in a staggered fashion. Opacity is not changed. The fade range is expressed in relation to the height of the map view. A value of 1.0 indicates that the content is faded to the same extent as the map’s height in pixels, while a value close to zero represents a sharp cutoff. When the value is set to 0.0, the cutoff is completely disabled. Note: The property has no effect on the map if terrain is enabled.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Default value: 0. Value range: [0, 1]","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.mapbox.MapboxMaps\/documentation\/MapboxMaps","doc:\/\/com.mapbox.MapboxMaps\/documentation\/MapboxMaps\/FillExtrusionLayer"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/mapboxmaps\/fillextrusionlayer\/fillextrusioncutofffaderange(_:)-2kfwa"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.mapbox.MapboxMaps\/documentation\/MapboxMaps\/FillExtrusionLayer\/fillExtrusionCutoffFadeRange(_:)-2kfwa","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"fillExtrusionCutoffFadeRange","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"constant","kind":"internalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10MapboxMaps18FillExtrusionLayerV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"FillExtrusionLayer","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.mapbox.MapboxMaps\/documentation\/MapboxMaps\/FillExtrusionLayer"}],"platforms":["iOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"name":"MapboxMaps"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"fillExtrusionCutoffFadeRange"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"text":"FillExtrusionLayer","preciseIdentifier":"s:10MapboxMaps18FillExtrusionLayerV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"externalID":"s:10MapboxMaps18FillExtrusionLayerV04fillD15CutoffFadeRangeyACSdF","extendedModule":"MapboxMaps","title":"fillExtrusionCutoffFadeRange(_:)","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method"},"references":{"doc://com.mapbox.MapboxMaps/documentation/MapboxMaps/FillExtrusionLayer/fillExtrusionCutoffFadeRange(_:)-2kfwa":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This parameter defines the range for the fade-out effect before an automatic content cutoff on pitched map views. Fade out is implemented by scaling down and removing buildings in the fade range in a staggered fashion. Opacity is not changed. The fade range is expressed in relation to the height of the map view. A value of 1.0 indicates that the content is faded to the same extent as the map’s height in pixels, while a value close to zero represents a sharp cutoff. When the value is set to 0.0, the cutoff is completely disabled. Note: The property has no effect on the map if terrain is enabled."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Default value: 0. Value range: [0, 1]","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"fillExtrusionCutoffFadeRange","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"text":"FillExtrusionLayer","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10MapboxMaps18FillExtrusionLayerV"}],"url":"\/documentation\/mapboxmaps\/fillextrusionlayer\/fillextrusioncutofffaderange(_:)-2kfwa","title":"